The React frontend displays the workspace and holds UI state. Its API client sends requests to FastAPI.
FastAPI routes handle project, dataset, run, result, layer, and report requests.
Application services save project and dataset information to the local filesystem. Project metadata is stored in JSON; datasets and run outputs are kept in project folders.
RunWorker submits analysis to a ThreadPoolExecutor. The current code configures two worker threads.
The GIS engine loads and validates the raster bands, aligns T1 and T2 for wetland analysis, applies the analysis-area masks, and runs vegetation inference.
ONNX Runtime runs the existing model on a five-channel tensor. The model predicts vegetation classes per pixel.
For wetland mode, the pipeline also computes temporal transitions, CVA, degradation/recovery, and water-related analysis. It calculates metrics and QA, then attempts to generate map figures and PDF reports.
The backend exposes results as JSON, map images, and report downloads. The map layer endpoint renders a raster as a PNG image; it is not shown in this code as a conventional XYZ tile service.
Vegetation mode follows the pipeline’s single-scene branch and does not do T1-versus-T2 change analysis. In wetland mode, the AI classifies both dates; GIS calculations compare those classifications and indices.


